# What `docker build .` never sends to the builder (v0.20.0 T18, spec §8.1).
# tests/test_deploy_files.py parses this file: every secret and runtime path
# below must stay excluded. The Dockerfile also COPYs only what the image
# runs, by name, so this list is the second of two fences, not the only one.

# History, tooling and working notes.
.git
.github
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.claude
.remember
.superpowers
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.log

# Environments and the client's toolchain (the built client is committed
# under content/scenes/clockwork/static/dist and copied with content/).
.venv
venv
**/node_modules
ui/

# The suite, the docs and the design sources: not run in the image.
tests/
docs/
Design_files/
models/

# Runtime data: the image's /data is a volume, never a layer.
data/
games/*/data/lore/*.db

# Secrets: reach a container only through its environment or files on /data.
config/local.yaml
config/secrets.yaml
llm_api_key.txt
lmstudio.txt
*.key
**/*.key
*.token
**/*.token
.env*
**/.env*
